{{also|Ballerina}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʷelH-}}
Borrowed from {{der|en|it|ballerina}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌbæləɹˈiːnə/}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːnə|s=4}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|ballerine}}

# A female [[ballet dancer]].
# The star female [[ballet]] [[performer]] in the company.
# {{lb|en|less common|non-standard}} A male ballet dancer; a [[ballerino]]
# A [[ballet flat]] [[shoe]].

====Usage notes====
Although normally used to refer only to females, it can be used of males although this is sometimes done so derogatorily. ''[[danseur]]'' or ''[[ballet dancer]]'' is the normal term for men.

